WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:06.060
In the mid-1800s, a group of archaeologists
from England embarked on an expedition to

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.210
Mongolia.

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:12.430
The expedition was headed by Jonathan Davis,
his long-term research partner Jason Porter,

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:14.889
and their assistant, Marvin Thomas.

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:19.810
With them, they brought a ship, all the necessary
equipment, and a team of ten workers to aid

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:23.779
with the dig and the transportation of any
relics back to the British Isles.

00:00:23.779 --> 00:00:28.640
There, they found a number of historically
significant artifacts, one of which was described

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:32.740
in Davis’s journal as
“A most marvelous discovery the likes of

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:34.530
which the world has never known!

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:39.840
It will surely be regarded as the crown jewel
of our findings, and I delight at the thought

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.820
of what ancient secrets it may allow us to
uncover!”

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.190
Unfortunately for him, he would never get
to find out.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:51.700
When the ship arrived back on the shores of
England, those waiting for its return discovered

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:54.350
that every single man on board was dead.

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:58.420
Their mangled bodies littered the deck of
the ship, and Johnathan Davis’s head had

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.239
been torn clean off.

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:05.280
Whatever had killed them, it was far stronger
than all thirteen men combined.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.029
Given the unusual circumstances of these deaths,
the artifacts were seized by The Oddities,

00:01:10.029 --> 00:01:16.140
Occult, and Paranormal Society, or OOPS - one
of the many groups started by stuffy English

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:21.459
gentlemen of the era that mainly functioned
as a glorified cabinet of curiosities - and

00:01:21.459 --> 00:01:23.439
placed in their Inner Sanctum.

00:01:23.439 --> 00:01:28.359
The largest, and most impressive of these,
was a large black stone cube, covered with

00:01:28.359 --> 00:01:34.590
strange symbols, which they displayed prominently
for several years, until one day, the same

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:40.990
dark force that killed the archaeologists
on their own ship stirred once more.

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:46.030
Something escaped from within the stone, killing
everyone present in the Inner Sanctum and

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:51.340
leaving a trail of more bodies in its wake
until eventually, it was apprehended by the

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:57.639
SCP Foundation, placed in containment, and
designated SCP-076.

00:01:57.639 --> 00:02:06.020
SCP-076 consists of two separate components:
a stone cube, SCP-076-1, and the humanoid

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:10.719
contained inside of the cube, or SCP-076-2.

00:02:10.719 --> 00:02:18.620
SCP-076-1 is a three-meter cube of black metamorphic
stone, covered in patterned engravings that

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:21.750
have not been matched to any known civilization.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:27.099
Analysis via radioisotope suggests that the
cube is at least ten thousand years old, though

00:02:27.099 --> 00:02:30.010
an exact date of origin could not be determined.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:35.230
There is a door on one side, sealed with a
lock surrounded by twenty smaller locks, all

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:37.659
arranged in a circular pattern.

00:02:37.659 --> 00:02:42.010
The Foundation has not been able to locate
any of the keys, and therefore is unable to

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:43.409
lock the door.

00:02:43.409 --> 00:02:48.590
This is unfortunate, given the nature of the
figure that lurks inside the cube, chained

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:51.300
inside of a stone coffin.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:58.269
This is the resting place of SCP-076-2, also
known as Able.

00:02:58.269 --> 00:03:02.540
Able is a humanoid male who appears to be
in his late twenties, with black hair, gray

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:04.340
eyes, and olive skin.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:08.319
In spite of his youthful appearance, his age
is estimated to be around the same as the

00:03:08.319 --> 00:03:09.950
cube that holds him.

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:14.760
His body is covered in tattoos, depicting
various occult icons and images of demonic

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.040
faces - not uncommon for warrior castes of
old.

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:23.730
When he is encased in his coffin, within his
stone prison, Able is technically dead and

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:26.650
registers no vital signs of any kind.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:29.439
However, he does not stay dead.

00:03:29.439 --> 00:03:34.810
On an occasional basis, with no apparent cause,
he will wake up and reanimate.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:39.819
Once he is awake and aware, he will attempt
to leave the cube by any means necessary.

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:44.230
If he manages to escape, he will look for
the nearest human being and attempt to kill

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:45.230
them.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:49.819
Once he has latched on to a target, he will
enter a rage state that will not stop until

00:03:49.819 --> 00:03:50.980
he is killed.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:56.530
Though, as his anomalous nature implies, this
death is never permanent, and he will always

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:58.879
awaken again eventually.

00:03:58.879 --> 00:04:03.730
Terminating Able in order to stopone of his
rampages is often difficult, as he possesses

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:07.780
strength and durability far beyond the capabilities
of an ordinary man.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:13.129
He has superhuman power and speed, and, though
his physical body can be damaged, he does

00:04:13.129 --> 00:04:17.569
not appear to respond to pain and continues
to fight through extreme injuries that would

00:04:17.569 --> 00:04:19.739
take most targets down.

00:04:19.739 --> 00:04:23.860
During his time in Foundation custody, he
has displayed the following abilities:

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:27.380
Over the course of four minutes, while trying
to attack a Research Assistant that happened

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:32.289
to cross into his line of sight moments before,
he ripped through a reinforced steel security

00:04:32.289 --> 00:04:37.539
door with his bare hands, breaking the steel
apart as if it were layers of tin foil.

00:04:37.539 --> 00:04:41.789
During another incident, he was able to run
a distance of 64 meters in under three seconds

00:04:41.789 --> 00:04:45.440
to catch up to an armored van filled with
Foundation guards.

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:50.030
While security staff attempted to neutralize
him during the same incident, he took several

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:55.199
.50 caliber rounds to the head and continued
to move and kill for several minutes after,

00:04:55.199 --> 00:05:00.090
in spite of having literal holes in his head
and missing portions of vital brain matter.

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:04.259
During another escape, he got ahold of a piece
of steel rebar which he used to swat bullets

00:05:04.259 --> 00:05:09.099
from handguns and assault rifles out of the
air, like he was batting a ball with a tennis

00:05:09.099 --> 00:05:10.099
racket.

00:05:10.099 --> 00:05:14.600
During another attempted escape, after killing
a half dozen D-Classes along the way, Foundation

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:19.390
staff were eventully able to trap the entity
in a vat of water, sealing the top, where

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:23.900
he tread water furiously for an hour before
eventually suffocating.

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:28.479
This suggests that, unlike most people who
will asphyxiate after only a few minutes without

00:05:28.479 --> 00:05:31.870
oxygen, he can survive for at least an hour.

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:36.290
The most notable of his anomalous skills,
however, is his ability to produce weapons,

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:39.970
usually bladed, from thin air whenever he
wants to.

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:43.819
Slowed-down security footage has shown that
he does this by pulling the weapons out of

00:05:43.819 --> 00:05:48.090
a tiny rift in space, a portal to another
dimension of some kind.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:53.770
It is unsure where this portal leads to, or
how Able accesses it, but it appears to function

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:59.340
as his own personal armory, stocked with an
endless supply of black, non-reflective bladed

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:03.280
weapons, which vanish as soon as they leave
his grasp.

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:08.420
Though it is difficult and often dangerous
to do so, Able can in fact be killed.

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:13.030
Some previously effective methods of termination
have included: fire from multiple heavy-caliber

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:19.490
machine guns, suffocation, being crushed beneath
a 13.6 metric ton piece of elevator equipment,

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:23.800
cremation via a grenade placed inside of a
cavity in his chest, and the detonation of

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:26.130
an on-site nuclear warhead.

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:32.690
Every time SCP-076-2 is killed, his corpse
quickly decays at an unnaturally rapid rate

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:35.379
until it has turned into a pile of dust.

00:06:35.379 --> 00:06:40.010
Then, the door to the cube, as well as the
coffin inside, will slam shut, and the lock

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:42.090
on the outside will rotate shut.

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:45.710
Somehow, Able’s body will then reform inside
the coffin.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:50.110
This process can take anywhere from six hours
to over 20 years.

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:55.240
After a series of failed experiments, containment
procedures for SCP-076 were amended to the

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:57.460
current procedures in place.

00:06:57.460 --> 00:07:03.990
SCP-076 is placed in Containment Area 25b,
located 200 meters below sea level, tunneled

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:07.590
into solid bedrock in an area with limited
seismic activity.

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:12.310
The only way to access this area is via an
elevator shaft, which is broken up every 50

00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:16.990
meters with a reinforced blast door made of
shielding that is 20 cm thick.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:21.129
When the elevator shaft is not being used,
it is flooded with seawater.

00:07:21.129 --> 00:07:25.789
The containment area includes an outer security
perimeter outfitted with security personnel

00:07:25.789 --> 00:07:30.940
trained in counter-intrusion and close-quarters
combat, an Administrative and Support area

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:35.389
where on-site personnel can live and rest,
a Primary Containment Zone filled with seawater

00:07:35.389 --> 00:07:41.740
and made of a 7m cube encased in reinforced
material, and then, a “killing corridor”

00:07:41.740 --> 00:07:47.530
that is 150 meters in size, with an electrical
system able to deliver a 20,000-volt shock

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:50.310
in the event of an attempted containment breach.

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:54.229
The security station at the entrance of the
killing corridor must be staffed with at least

00:07:54.229 --> 00:07:57.139
three armed security guards at all times.

00:07:57.139 --> 00:08:01.569
In the event of a containment breach, all
staff on-site must go to the closest security

00:08:01.569 --> 00:08:03.990
station immediately for weapons and armor.

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:08.819
The staff will remain at Alert Condition One
until Able has been neutralized and re-contained.

00:08:08.819 --> 00:08:14.199
If 90 minutes pass after a full breach without
the order to Stand Down being given, the entire

00:08:14.199 --> 00:08:19.710
facility will be flooded with seawater and
the access shaft will be sealed for 24 hours.

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:25.360
This is considered an extreme measure, as
it will kill any site staff present, but desperate

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:27.889
times call for desperate measures.

00:08:27.889 --> 00:08:32.840
After the containment procedures were amended,
and the file updated, Dr [Redacted] submitted

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:37.770
a complaint to Director Maria Jones, head
of Recordkeeping and Information Security

00:08:37.770 --> 00:08:38.920
Administration.

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:42.730
The correspondence reads as follows:
“I have to go on record as saying that I

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:48.080
seriously object to the proposed revisions
of the SCP-076 Special Containment Procedures

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:49.080
File.

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:53.160
I know that Redact All Important Stuff Already
claims it's a security risk, but you and I

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:57.940
both know it's just top brass trying to sweep
their biggest and most embarrassing mistake

00:08:57.940 --> 00:08:59.650
ever under the rug.

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:00.960
Omega-Seven happened.

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:02.270
It existed.

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:07.290
Those people died because you screwed up,
and you can't change that, no matter how hard

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:08.750
you try to hide it.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:12.620
For God's sake, man, those people guarding
him deserve to know exactly what he is and

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:13.860
what he did.

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:15.970
What WE did.

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:18.350
How we screwed up, so they'll know better.”

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:20.590
So what was Omega-Seven?

00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:25.390
What could have possibly constituted one of
the Foundation’s worst, greatest, most humiliating

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:27.430
mistakes ever?

00:09:27.430 --> 00:09:31.700
Following the death of an Agent, whose identity
has been redacted, who had managed to best

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:37.150
Able several times in combat, the Foundation
became aware of an intriguing possibility:

00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:41.920
Whenever Able encountered the rare individual
he perceived as superior, or at least equal,

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:46.720
to him in combat, his uncontrollable rage
would subside and he would develop a kind

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:47.880
of respect.

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:52.350
When Able learned of the man’s death, he
calmed down and was coherent enough to interview.

00:09:52.350 --> 00:09:56.670
He was distressed at the death, which had
occurred as collateral damage in an airstrike

00:09:56.670 --> 00:09:59.450
intended to contain another SCP.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:04.230
He explained his feelings on the subject:
“A man like that deserves to die in combat,

00:10:04.230 --> 00:10:07.050
so close to his opponent he can feel his breath.

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:12.810
Not in some destruction ordered by cowardly
kings and princes safe in their palaces.

00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:15.480
The rest of you…you disgust me.

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:18.290
I don't even have the urge to strike you down.”

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:22.850
After this interview, the Researcher who conducted
it recommended that the Foundation attempt

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:27.940
to find a way to work with Able, and somehow
militarize him in accordance with the Bowe

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:32.210
Commission’s desire to use SCP objects for
tactical purposes.

00:10:32.210 --> 00:10:38.830
A Mobile Task Force was proposed, referred
to as “Omega-7” or by its nickname “Pandora’s

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:39.940
Box.”

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:45.050
Task Force Omega-Seven was to consist of between
ten and twenty field agents, split up into

00:10:45.050 --> 00:10:47.770
teams of three and five people each.

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:53.160
Members of these teams have selected a roster
of highly qualified field agents, and chosen

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:55.130
by Able himself.

00:10:55.130 --> 00:11:00.100
Their purpose would be to provide support
to him during high-risk fieldwork and combat-based

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:01.100
situations.

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:05.380
Able was outfitted with a device attached
to his neck that, if it was triggered or interfered

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:10.610
with in any way, would detonate and destroy
his spinal cord, trachea, and the major blood

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:13.440
vessels of his neck, killing him instantly.

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:17.810
A tracking device was also attached to Able,
in order to keep the Foundation informed of

00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:19.850
his whereabouts at all times.

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:24.660
Able was instructed to refrain from any unnecessary
killing or violence, and only attack when

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:25.660
ordered to.

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:30.410
This operation was off to a bit of a rocky
start, and the head researcher in charge of

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:33.600
it added this addendum to the initial project
proposal:

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:36.940
“For God's sake, find these guys something
to do.

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:41.480
Able's getting bored, and he's started putting
his team through live-fire exercises: they

00:11:41.480 --> 00:11:43.390
get bullets, he gets training weapons.

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:47.140
Have you ever seen someone break a man's jaw
using a Nerf sword?

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:49.140
He's not gonna stop until someone gets killed.”

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:53.570
Indeed, Able was getting restless, and the
Foundation needed to find a way to keep him

00:11:53.570 --> 00:11:57.530
busy until he could be occupied with bloodier
pursuits.

00:11:57.530 --> 00:12:00.340
This project report was submitted regarding
Able’s activities:

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:06.060
“In light of SCP-076-2's proficient use
of the Sumerian language, researchers have

00:12:06.060 --> 00:12:08.270
asked it to translate several documents.

00:12:08.270 --> 00:12:12.650
While it originally replied with disinterest,
it has translated some of the documents it

00:12:12.650 --> 00:12:14.740
found worthy of its attention.

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:20.450
Most of the documents chosen by SCP-076-2
were regarding battles or legendary heroes,

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:24.070
one of its favorites in particular being the
"Epic of Gilgamesh".

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:28.660
However, one researcher presented it with
the symbol from SCP-073.

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:34.740
Upon sight of this, SCP-076-2 became highly
enraged, killing several of the researchers

00:12:34.740 --> 00:12:37.330
before its kill switch could be activated.

00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:43.570
When revived and questioned about this, SCP-076-2
responded aggressively, and that line of questioning

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:45.190
was immediately dropped.

00:12:45.190 --> 00:12:52.260
It is recommended anything pertaining to SCP-073
never be brought to the attention of SCP-076-2

00:12:52.260 --> 00:12:55.510
and that the two are never to be in the same
facility.”

00:12:55.510 --> 00:13:00.340
Eventually, the chance to see Omega-Seven
in action came about, and Able and his task

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:02.890
force were deployed at the request of the
Bowe Commission.

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:07.100
Though the details have been redacted from
the official file, the mission was deemed

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:12.010
a success, and General Bowe thanked the research
team in an email with the subject line “A

00:13:12.010 --> 00:13:13.200
Job Well Done”.

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:15.450
He wrote: “Excellent work, doctor.

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:17.460
The mission went exactly as expected.

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:19.900
We'll be calling you again if we need your
help.”

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:24.050
This new chapter of the project bred discord
between the two lead researchers assigned

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:30.360
to Able, from here on referred to as Dr. W
and Dr. P. Dr. P was highly in favor of Omega-Seven

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:35.520
and its military applications, while Dr. W
strongly disapproved, believing the project

00:13:35.520 --> 00:13:40.200
to be an example of the military forcing the
SCP Foundation to do its dirty work.

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:44.610
He responded to the General’s congratulations
with a strongly worded email to his colleague,

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:46.800
too strongly worded to repeat here.

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:50.100
To summarize it neatly: he was very upset.

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:56.290
Following this email, and at Dr. P’s request,
Dr. W was reassigned to SCP-682, leaving him

00:13:56.290 --> 00:13:59.870
as the sole researcher in charge of the Omega-Seven
project.

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:03.910
After a series of incidents regarding friendly
fire and casualties within the task force

00:14:03.910 --> 00:14:09.220
itself, most of which occurred during ordinary
combat training, Dr. P sent an email to the

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:11.730
General:
“Despite our best efforts, Subject Able

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:13.260
is proving difficult to control.

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:17.970
All our attempts to keep him engaged have
been more or less unsuccessful.

00:14:17.970 --> 00:14:22.020
The problem is, he's a perfect killing machine,
and that's all he wants to do.

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:26.660
Which seems like exactly what we wanted, but
the problem is, we can't seem to turn him

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:27.660
off.

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:31.470
I'm running out of missions to give him, and
the ones I've got left aren't engaging him

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:32.470
mentally.

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:34.580
He's starting to lash out at the other team
members.

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:37.210
It's only a matter of time before something
goes wrong.

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:41.760
Requesting permission to discontinue the project
and neutralize Able temporarily, until we

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:43.930
can find something more for him to do.”

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:47.300
The General refused to agree to this: “Unacceptable.

00:14:47.300 --> 00:14:51.070
Neutralizing Subject Able at this point is
going to cause us an unacceptable delay.

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:53.430
We'll have another mission for you within
a couple of weeks.

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:56.070
All you have to do is keep him busy until
then.

00:14:56.070 --> 00:14:57.900
Send him on vacation or something.”

00:14:57.900 --> 00:15:03.010
Dr. P was stunned by this response, and unsure
how to proceed.

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:07.230
Not only was there nowhere safe to send Able
on vacation, short of firing him into the

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:11.770
furthest recesses of outer space where he
could not hurt anyone, he was simply not a

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:16.040
man interested in leisure, rest, or vacation
as a concept.

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:22.220
They had let the tiger out of its cage, and
now all it wanted to do was shred, bite, and

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:23.220
kill.

00:15:23.220 --> 00:15:27.450
He tried to keep Able occupied, burning through
D-Class on a daily basis that he could use

00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:31.810
as human practice dummies, but eventually
Able’s craving for a challenge became too

00:15:31.810 --> 00:15:32.980
strong.

00:15:32.980 --> 00:15:37.350
An automated alert went out to the staff of
the site where Able was contained, signaling

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:39.150
the start of a state of emergency:
“SCP-076-2 has disabled the explosive collar

00:15:39.150 --> 00:15:40.570
failsafe and gone out of control.

00:15:40.570 --> 00:15:44.800
All staff to high alert.

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:50.940
Further requests as events warrant.”

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:54.820
There is no surviving security footage from
this incident, and there are no witnesses

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:56.790
to recount what happened next.

00:15:56.790 --> 00:16:01.920
Here is what we know for sure: Sometime after
Able escaped from his explosive collar, Containment

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:06.410
Area 25 began the ten-minute countdown for
its on-site nuclear warhead.

00:16:06.410 --> 00:16:10.630
No staff were able to successfully evacuate
before the warhead detonated, reducing the

00:16:10.630 --> 00:16:12.130
site to rubble.

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:16.780
Site 67 and 68 activated FEMA protocol and
secured the location.

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:21.510
Meanwhile, the stone coffin sealed itself
again, the lock clicked shut, and Able began

00:16:21.510 --> 00:16:23.690
to rebuild from almost nothing.

00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:26.680
Ashes to ashes, as they say.

00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:28.960
And dust to dust.

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:33.610
Following this, a revised psychological profile
of the entity was submitted:

00:16:33.610 --> 00:16:39.530
“SCP-076-2 either possesses a mind constructed
much differently than our own, or is completely

00:16:39.530 --> 00:16:44.170
insane, with little empathy or ideas in a
way that we would understand it.

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:50.551
Concepts such as sex, love, and equality are
completely foreign ideas to SCP-076-2, or

00:16:50.551 --> 00:16:53.520
at least in comparison to its way of viewing
them.

00:16:53.520 --> 00:16:58.370
Subject has shown that it is completely disinterested
in sex, barely differentiating between genders

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:00.700
except as a form of visual identification.

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:05.399
Also, while subject seems to greatly enjoy
the act of killing, causing pain - either

00:17:05.399 --> 00:17:09.169
emotionally or physically - holds no attraction
to it.

00:17:09.169 --> 00:17:15.279
Intelligence tests have been wildly inconclusive
when applied to SCP-076-2, and no accurate

00:17:15.279 --> 00:17:17.549
result has yet been obtained.

00:17:17.549 --> 00:17:22.220
This is due to the fact that no communication
is possible with the Subject when in its "rage"

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:23.220
state.

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:27.209
Subject displays knowledge of several languages
including English, but most notable is its

00:17:27.209 --> 00:17:32.580
knowledge of several dialects of ancient Sumerian,
which seem to be its preferred language.

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:38.000
SCP-076 has nothing but contempt for human
beings and will kill them on sight.

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:40.750
No communication is to be attempted with the
subject.”

00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:46.649
Now go check out “SCP-001 - Dark Truth About
The O5 Council” and “Top 15 Most Dangerous

00:17:46.649 --> 00:17:52.179
SCP Monsters in Containment” for more deadly
secrets from inside the Foundation!

